<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Illustrative Examples</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Example for Pareto-Nash Equilibrium</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For example, consider a two agent two objective game. Each agent follows a Gaussian policy with fixed variance, <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mu_{1},1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mu_{1},1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{2}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mu_{2},1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{2}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mu_{2},1)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{1},\mu_{2}\in[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{1},\mu_{2}\in[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. Define team reward as</p>
<table id="A3.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(r_{1},r_{2})=\left(\exp\!\left[-\tfrac{1}{2}\Big((a_{1}-1)^{2}+\tfrac{1}{2}(a_{2}-1)^{2}\Big)\right],\;\exp\!\left[-\tfrac{1}{2}\Big(\tfrac{1}{2}(a_{1}+1)^{2}+2(a_{2}+1)^{2}\Big)\right]\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(r_{1},r_{2})=\left(\exp\!\left[-\tfrac{1}{2}\Big((a_{1}-1)^{2}+\tfrac{1}{2}(a_{2}-1)^{2}\Big)\right],\;\exp\!\left[-\tfrac{1}{2}\Big(\tfrac{1}{2}(a_{1}+1)^{2}+2(a_{2}+1)^{2}\Big)\right]\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In this example, every policy parametrized by <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mu_{1},\mu_{2})\in[-1,1]^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mu_{1},\mu_{2})\in[-1,1]^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is a Pareto–Nash equilibrium, since any unilateral change that improves one objective necessarily decreases the other. However, most of these equilibria are not pareto optimal</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>A Toy Example of Better Team Improvement with Agent-specific Preferences</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide a simple two-agent Gaussian policy example to illustrate why diverse preferences can induce better team solutions than a single shared preference. Each agent uses a Gaussian policy with fixed variance:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}\sim\pi_{i}(\cdot;\mu_{i})=\mathcal{N}(\mu_{i},\sigma),\qquad i\in\{1,2\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}\sim\pi_{i}(\cdot;\mu_{i})=\mathcal{N}(\mu_{i},\sigma),\qquad i\in\{1,2\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the only optimizable parameter. Let
<math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{i}\in[-1.5,1.5]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1.5</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1.5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{i}\in[-1.5,1.5]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and define the expected team return as
<math id="A3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(\mu)=\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi_{\mu}}[r(a)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\mu)=\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi_{\mu}}[r(a)]</annotation></semantics></math>, where
<math id="A3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(a)=(r_{1}(a),r_{2}(a))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(a)=(r_{1}(a),r_{2}(a))</annotation></semantics></math>. Agent <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> and agent <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> use preferences</p>
<table id="A3.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{1}=(\alpha,1-\alpha),\qquad w_{2}=(\beta,1-\beta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{1}=(\alpha,1-\alpha),\qquad w_{2}=(\beta,1-\beta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The reward components are</p>
<table id="A3.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}(a_{1},a_{2})=\frac{1}{\sqrt{3}}\exp\left(-\frac{(a_{1}-1)^{2}}{4}-\frac{(a_{2}-1)^{2}}{6}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}(a_{1},a_{2})=\frac{1}{\sqrt{3}}\exp\left(-\frac{(a_{1}-1)^{2}}{4}-\frac{(a_{2}-1)^{2}}{6}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A3.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{2}(a_{1},a_{2})=\frac{1}{\sqrt{4.5}}\exp\left(-\frac{(a_{1}+1)^{2}}{6}-\frac{(a_{2}+1)^{2}}{3}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>4.5</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{2}(a_{1},a_{2})=\frac{1}{\sqrt{4.5}}\exp\left(-\frac{(a_{1}+1)^{2}}{6}-\frac{(a_{2}+1)^{2}}{3}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Starting from the same initial policy mean <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{0}=(0,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{0}=(0,0)</annotation></semantics></math>, we compare
gradient ascent under a shared preference and under agent-specific preferences.
With <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{1}=w_{2}=(0.5,0.5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{1}=w_{2}=(0.5,0.5)</annotation></semantics></math>, the trajectory converges to
<math id="A3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\mathrm{shared}}=(-1.000,-1.000)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>shared</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1.000</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1.000</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathrm{shared}}=(-1.000,-1.000)</annotation></semantics></math>, with
<math id="A3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(\mu_{\mathrm{shared}})=(0.905,0.905)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>shared</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.905</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.905</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\mu_{\mathrm{shared}})=(0.905,0.905)</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A3.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{\mathrm{team}}=0.905" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>team</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.905</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{\mathrm{team}}=0.905</annotation></semantics></math>. In contrast, with agent-specific preferences
<math id="A3.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{1}=(1.000,0.000)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1.000</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.000</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{1}=(1.000,0.000)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{2}=(0.000,1.000)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.000</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.000</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{2}=(0.000,1.000)</annotation></semantics></math>, the trajectory converges to
<math id="A3.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\mathrm{agent}}=(1.000,1.000)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>agent</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1.000</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.000</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathrm{agent}}=(1.000,1.000)</annotation></semantics></math>, with
<math id="A3.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(\mu_{\mathrm{agent}})=(1.105,1.105)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>agent</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1.105</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.105</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\mu_{\mathrm{agent}})=(1.105,1.105)</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A3.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{\mathrm{team}}=1.105" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>team</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.105</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{\mathrm{team}}=1.105</annotation></semantics></math>, where
<math id="A3.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{\mathrm{team}}(R)=\frac{1}{2}(R_{1}+R_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>team</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{\mathrm{team}}(R)=\frac{1}{2}(R_{1}+R_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, agent-specific preferences improve the final team utility by <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.200" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.200</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.200</annotation></semantics></math>,
or approximately <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="22.1\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>22.1</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">22.1\%</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
